--- !u!114 &23594621
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 23594618}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 19ca26facb647c443aef5d9d594c0523, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  rules: '<b>How to Play 8 Ball Pool</b>


    <b>Objective:</b> The objective of
    8 Ball Pool is to pot your designated balls (stripes or solids) and then pot
    the 8 ball to win the game.


    <b>Setup:</b> The game starts with the balls
    arranged in a triangle with the 8 ball in the center.


    <b>1. Break Shot:</b>
    The player who breaks must strike the cue ball with the cue stick, aiming to
    hit the triangular rack of balls. The break should scatter the balls.


    <b>2.
    Choosing Groups:</b> After the break, the first player to pot a ball chooses
    either the solid balls or the striped balls to pot.


    <b>3. Taking Turns:</b>
    Players take turns trying to pot their designated balls. On each turn, the player
    must strike the cue ball, aiming for their designated group.


    <b>4. Potting
    Balls:</b> If the player pots a ball from their group, they continue their turn.
    If they miss or commit a foul, the opponent takes their turn.


    <b>5. Potting
    the 8 Ball:</b> Once all balls from a player''s group are potted, they can attempt
    to pot the 8 ball. The player must call their shot before attempting to pot the
    8 ball.


    <b>Winning the Game:</b> The game is won by potting the 8 ball
    after all your designated balls have been potted. However, potting the 8 ball
    prematurely or committing a foul when trying to pot the 8 ball results in a loss.


    <b>Fouls:</b>
    Common fouls include scratching the cue ball, potting the cue ball, or hitting
    the wrong ball first.


    <b>Good Luck and Enjoy the Game!</b>'
